WIRE.md §6.5, ERRORS.md W7115 "looping": a mutual link chain (a -> b -> a) never resolves; the
archive's own memFS (findings_test.go, itself hop-bounded) reports project.ErrSymlinkLoop, which
load maps here (project's own resolver gets the equivalent evalSymlinksOS test in
internal/project). Both names in the chain match the glob and are classified independently, so
each is reported once.
-- pattern --
data/*.json
-- data/a.json --
{"label": "a"}
-- symlinks --
data/loop1.json /p/data/loop2.json
data/loop2.json /p/data/loop1.json
-- findings.txt --
warning[W7115]  pattern:1:1
  symbolic link data/loop1.json is part of a loop; skipped

warning[W7115]  pattern:1:1
  symbolic link data/loop2.json is part of a loop; skipped

0 errors, 2 warnings in 1 package (…)
